        "agenda_item_number": "7.",
        "title": "Inquiries",
        "attachments": [],
        "description": "",
        "minutes": "Member Carr \u2013 Roles and Responsibilities Regarding Business Plan Development\nThe Ottawa Police Services Board Policy Manual notes:\n[T]he Ottawa Police Services Board is required by subsection 32(1) of Ontario Regulation 3/99 (\" the Adequacy Standards\") to enter into a protocol with the Council for the Municipality of Ottawa that addresses:\nA. The sharing of information with Municipal Council, including the type of information to be shared and the frequency of sharing such information.\u00a0B. The dates by which the business plan and annual report shall be provided to Municipal Council.\u00a0C. The responsibility for making public the business plan and annual report and the dates by which the business plan and report must be made public.\u00a0D. If the Municipal Council chooses, jointly determining, and participating in, the consultation processes for the development of the business plan.\nCan staff clearly outline the respective roles and authorities of the Police Services Board and Ottawa City Council concerning the development of the Police Services\u2019 Business Plan.",
        "motions": []
      },
